    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-12T09:33:46+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T09:33:46+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T23:03:46Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T23:03:46Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough located about northern parts of SA continues crossing the state and will clear to the northeast during the day. A cool southwesterly airstream will follow as a high pressure system drifts eastwards across the Bight early this week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 24 to 33.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h turning southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Leigh Creek, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek. Winds southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the morning. Sunny day. Winds southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
